Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: log normal ACL sends at info level

An ordinary connected ACL send is not a warning. Logging every successful
GATT response at warning level can overwrite fault records in a bounded
RAM log when informational tracing is disabled. Retain the diagnostic at
info level, consistent with other normal connection traffic. No controller,
buffer, retry or connection behavior changes.

diff --git a/wireless/bluetooth/bt_conn.c b/wireless/bluetooth/bt_conn.c
--- a/wireless/bluetooth/bt_conn.c
+++ b/wireless/bluetooth/bt_conn.c
@@ -437,7 +437,7 @@ void bt_conn_send(FAR struct bt_conn_s *conn, FAR struct bt_buf_s *buf)
 
   sq_init(&fraglist);
 
-  wlwarn("conn handle %u buf len %u\n", conn->handle, buf->len);
+  wlinfo("conn handle %u buf len %u\n", conn->handle, buf->len);
 
   if (conn->state != BT_CONN_CONNECTED)
     {
